Server managers let FOSSBilling create, suspend, unsuspend, and manage hosting accounts through external control panels or provisioning backends.

Review your control panel's supported actions before relying on automatic provisioning in production.

## Supported Integrations

- [CWP](/admin-guide/server-managers/cwp/)
- [DirectAdmin](https://www.directadmin.com/)
- [HestiaCP](/admin-guide/server-managers/hestiacp/)
- [Plesk](https://www.plesk.com/) — FOSSBilling assigns the named plan when creating a subscription. Package changes update the settings on an existing subscription. To switch its assigned plan, use Plesk.
- [WHM/cPanel](/admin-guide/server-managers/whm/)

For other control panels, see [requested integrations](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/issues/1362) or follow the guide to [creating a server manager](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-server-manager/).

## Add a Hosting Server

{% steps %}
1. Set up API access in your control panel.
2. In the FOSSBilling admin panel, go to **System → Hosting Plans and Servers** and select **New Server**
3. Enter the server name, hostname, and IP address. Add the nameservers your hosting accounts should use, if applicable.
4. Under **Connection Settings**, select the **Server Manager** and enter any credentials it requires. Set **Connection Port** if your panel uses a custom port.
5. Select **Add Server**
{% /steps %}
